Design for Ease of Recycling ensures that products can be efficiently processed through existing or emerging recycling infrastructure at end of life. This means selecting materials that are widely recyclable, avoiding material combinations that contaminate recycling streams, designing for easy material identification and separation, and considering the practical constraints of recycling facilities — sorting capabilities, processing temperatures, and contamination tolerances. Products that are easy to recycle retain more material value and divert less waste to landfill or incineration.